Surface nature:  CONTROLLED, storage-agnostic PRESENTATIONAL primitive. The web source's own doc comment states
                 "Persists nothing on its own — DataTable owns persistence via tableId." It receives `columns` +
                 `visibleKeys` as plain props and renders an icon-button trigger + a click-dismissed popover;
                 there is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise. So it has NO loading / error / stale /
                 offline branch (nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect). Reproduced branches = the source's
                 REAL ones: closed (only the trigger renders), open with one+ column rows (each shown / hidden
                 via its checkbox, with the per-row guardrails: a required column is pinned visible, the last
                 visible column can't be hidden) plus the "Show all" control, and the empty column set (web
                 renders an empty list; natively a friendly empty body, never a blank box). No loading/error/
                 stale/offline chrome was fabricated — same faithful-parity stance as the sibling primitive
                 DataTableColumnMenu (0210). Browser facilities map to native peers: the controlled
                 `visibleKeys` + `onChange` -> @Observable DataTableColumnsMenuController owning the keys and
                 mirroring changes to a host callback; the `open` useState + click-outside/Escape dismiss ->
                 .popover with .presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover); <input type=checkbox> -> a HIG checkbox
                 Toggle (DataTableColumnsMenuCheckboxToggleStyle); the component toggle/showAll logic ->
                 the pure DataTableColumnsMenuProjector.

Data sources reproduced (from web source):
  • useTranslation                 -> DataTableColumnsMenuStrings facade (P1/S10), table "DataTableColumnsMenu"
